# Task 149-023 Execution Plan
## Goal
Create scripts/doc-review.mjs — a Node.js script that:
1. Lists all .md files in the workspace
2. Analyzes size, last-modified, sprint reference count
3. Detects duplicates (hash-based)
4. Checks for broken internal links
5. Applies stale heuristic (Sprint N where N < current-10 → REVISE)
6. Categorizes each file: KEEP / REVISE / DELETE / MOVE
7. Outputs docs/audits/sprint-149/doc-review-report.md

## Files to Create
- scripts/doc-review.mjs (NEW, ~200 LoC)
- docs/audits/sprint-149/doc-review-report.md (generated output)

## Approach
1. Use Node.js built-ins only (fs, path, crypto) — no external deps
2. Walk the repo to find all .md files
3. For each file: stat, read content, compute hash, extract sprint refs, check links
4. Deduplicate by hash
5. Apply category rules
6. Write markdown report with 4 sections: KEEP / REVISE / DELETE / MOVE

## Category Rules
- DELETE: empty files or near-duplicates (same hash as another)
- REVISE: contains old sprint refs (N < 149-10=139), or broken links
- MOVE: files in root that belong in docs/
- KEEP: everything else

## Test Criteria
1. Script runs without error → exit 0
2. Report has 4 category sections (## KEEP / ## REVISE / ## DELETE / ## MOVE)
3. Broken link detection works (at least finds and reports)
